  "majorLessons": [
    "A passing command is not a preservation proof: R6 remains STOP_POSTFLIGHT_UNVERIFIED despite four zero child exits.",
    "A diagnostic can authenticate known root drift without claiming historical root unchanged or inventing a new baseline.",
    "Use full retained-fact digest arithmetic rather than weakening metadata checks or rescanning private state during source review.",
    "Keep preparation60 separate from inherited launch330/active320/runner300; no combined parent timer is claimed.",
    "Preserve HOME in both executed and dormant source paths.",
    "Authenticate real consumer schemas and source-role maps; avoid guessed result structures and source/grant hash cycles."
  ],
  "preservedR1Finding": {
    "issue": "Inherited dormant run_child assigned HOME; fresh R2 removes that assignment. R1 remains immutable.",
